{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>In all toil</b> — stands in place of two, namely on account of all toil and labor that one exerts for his livelihood, there is gain and benefit, and <b>in the toil of lips' speech</b>, which are words of vanity, there is lack. And the meaning: that he lacks everything and has only a pittance left over from the toiler."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:48.744491035Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}